  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Story model and cross-links",
      "items": [
        "The live world object groups characters, three event scopes, locations, factions, items, lore, world rules and project metadata. Schemas define field types and permitted link targets. (data.js:1-22; schemas.js:1-38, 82-220)",
        "Records link by ID. Link previews resolve IDs against the selected target categories and navigate to the matching entry. (data.js:44-51; components.js:392-404; README.md:14-16)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Editing behavior",
      "items": [
        "Adding an entry creates a type-prefixed ID; duplication copies the record with a new ID. Delete keeps one last-deleted record for the undo action. (data.js:24-32; components.js:3-67)",
        "Field edits update the in-memory world and save when confirmed. Search filters the active collection; category navigation and linked IDs rerender and move to the selected entry. (components.js:69-100, 109-129; ui.js:3-95; README.md:15-17)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Import path and validation",
      "items": [
        "Pasted JSON and fetched JSON are parsed, checked for a valid world shape, normalized with missing collections and metadata defaults, then saved before the interface is refreshed. (storage.js:44-115, 118-199)",
        "Google Drive share URLs are converted to download URLs; GitHub blob URLs are changed to raw URLs. The browser rejects HTTP failures, HTML responses and invalid JSON structures before replacing the current world. (storage.js:54-114, 129-150; README.md:32-38)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Persistence and portability",
      "items": [
        "The world is stored under worldBuilderData in this browser. Missing or malformed saved data falls back to the sample template; clearing browser storage can remove the local copy. (storage.js:1-26; README.md:65-67)",
        "Export creates a JSON download, copies JSON to the clipboard with a legacy copy fallback, or opens a blob URL preview in a new tab. (storage.js:201-249; README.md:32-36)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Themes, direction and hosting",
      "items": [
        "The README lists 28 themes. Applying a theme changes CSS variables and the dark-theme class, then persists the chosen theme in world metadata. Text direction is stored under a separate localStorage key. (README.md:14-18; themes.js:238-274, 314-318)",
        "GitHub Pages hosts the static app. The Jekyll workflow runs a Docker build for main pushes and pull requests; its workflow file contains no deployment step. The app can also run from a local index.html without a package install or build step. (README.md:24-30; .github/workflows/jekyll-docker.yml:1-19)"
      ]
    }
  ]
